 1. Unit Testing (Foundation Layer)
What it is

Testing individual components in isolation:

Apex classes
Triggers
Utility methods
Goal

Validate business logic correctness

What to test (real-world)
All branches (if/else)
Null handling
Exception scenarios
Edge cases (empty lists, invalid inputs)
Example mindset
// Not just calling method
System.assertEquals(expected, actual);
Production Insight
Fastest tests
Run in every deployment
Should not depend on:
DB state
External systems
2. Integration Testing
What it is

Testing interaction between:

Salesforce ↔ External APIs
Salesforce ↔ Middleware (MuleSoft, etc.)
What to validate
Request structure (JSON/XML)
Response handling
Error handling (timeouts, 500 errors)
Salesforce Reality

You must mock using:

HttpCalloutMock
Example scenarios
Payment gateway
KYC verification API
ERP integration
Production Insight
Most bugs happen here (not unit tests)
Always test:
Success response
Failure response
Partial data
